From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FE Fates port <engine@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:45:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] page: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: presets, share code, the
 Esc window fits

Round 74 (docs/ROUND74_PLAN.md A6 and A9, docs/rando/FULL_BLOCK.md sections
6, 7 and 9, owner OK "Yes, start round 74"; preset contents and help lines are
the plan's calls 2 and 3, from Grok's proposal docs/collab/ROUND74_PRESETS_GROK.md).

Presets: rando.py schema gains a top-level "presets" list (format stays 1;
older pages ignore it). The page reads it (parse_presets, Found::presets) and
draws one grid row "Presets" in Basics under Randomizer with a button per
preset (targets btn:preset:<name>). A press (RandoForm::preset) puts every row
at its default, page-only switches too, sets the preset's values through
RandoForm::set (fixed and game-hidden rows keep their rule), keeps the seed box
and writes the preset's one help line. Presets are buttons, not rows: they never
enter the answer or the run id.

Share code: a Share code row under the seed (field row:share, buttons
btn:share:copy and btn:share:paste). The field shows the code of the form's
values; an empty seed box gives the proposed seed Start game would use; a seed
the randomizer does not take gives no code. Code: <head>-<body>-<check>-<seed>,
head = "R1" + game letter (F Fates, S Seal of Flames) + 2-character layout hash
of the share rows (every row not page-only and not the seed, sorted by key);
body = each row's value index bit-packed (number rows as value minus min),
Crockford base 32; check = fnv1a32(head-body-seed) & 0x3FF. The real schema
today: 56 share rows, 127 bits, 26 body characters, 44 characters with an
8-character seed, 68 with a 32-character one. share_encode / share_decode are
the twins of tools/randomizer/sharecode.py and are tested against the same
vectors (tests/rando_sharecode_vectors.json, found by walking up from the crate;
not found = the test fails). A code pasted into the field (Ctrl+V, or the page
robot's paste) is used at once; a typed one with Enter or Paste: the form is
reset to its defaults, every row set through RandoForm::set, the seed box set,
so the same code gives the same answer text and run id. A refused code changes
nothing and the help line shows its one plain sentence (not a share code / a
typo / another version of the randomizer / for the other game / damaged).
Copy puts the code out through egui (ctx.copy_text). Paste with nothing typed
empties the field and says to press Ctrl+V (the program reads no clipboard of
its own). The share code is never part of the answer.

The Esc window fits (A9): This run's list (changed rows and the core's
notices) is in its own scroll area capped at 15% of the screen (54 to 160
points), and the Next New Game rows take what is left after about 330 points
(at least 80, at most round 71's 35%), so at 800 x 480 with "Randomize
everything" listed (22 rows) Keep stays on the screen. The part's help line
rests on "Keep keeps this seed. For a new seed, clear the seed box before
Keep." (call 6). The presets and the Share code field show in the part too
(targets next:...).

Page robot hook: steps {"paste": text} (an egui paste event to the control
with the focus), {"paste_copied": true} (the text the page's last Copy put out,
logged as {"event": "copied"} from egui's copy command) and {"expect_target":
target} (the control drawn wholly on the 800 x 480 screen); click events carry
the field's code ("share"), expect events the help line's note.

Off means original: nothing here writes guest memory or changes what Start game
sends for the same values; without presets in the schema no preset row is drawn.
Frontend only (rando_page.rs, pagebot.rs). New tests presets_are_read_from_the_schema,
a_preset_resets_every_row_and_keeps_the_seed, share_codes_match_the_shared_vectors,
the_same_code_gives_the_same_answer_on_a_fresh_page,
preset_buttons_and_the_share_field_are_clicked_like_any_control,
keep_stays_on_a_short_screen_with_this_run_full, pagebot
the_robot_presses_presets_and_pastes_the_share_code and
the_robot_finds_keep_on_the_screen_with_this_run_full (cargo tests run in the
round's gate / B3, not by the track).
